" :question/math-academy-id "q-85080" :question/problem "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $5{x}^{2}+30x+2y+41=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $x$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+30x+2y+41 & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+30x & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5[{x}^{2}+6x] & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5[(x+3)^{2}-9] & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2}-45 & =-2y-41 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2} & =-2y-41+45 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2} & =-2y+4 \\\\ 5(x+3)^{2} & =-2(y-2) \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =-\\frac{2}{5}(y-2) \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{10})(y-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(-3,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "744f58f2-59be-552a-bb2f-d0819f35c1ca"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11884/selection/8e581b09527373b2c046d3c04ffa0d440c27569eeb5d9ffd3f615d6875c22ec0" :answer/id #uuid "a8d1da2b-2d72-59ef-a792-bb85c1eb223e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11884/selection/7209a43b6c2b5cd8e9c292ea9df705bd6ad91c4f5f412791404f866b94343db5" :answer/id #uuid "9c5c5924-7b06-51c0-af6c-5c3162d97a97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11884/selection/45204ae0c76cd23d55c6fc0e092c448b5bd8159be1c575530b4166fe31d349c5" :answer/id #uuid "bf3b9416-3fe8-51e8-855f-fe197b979580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11884/selection/fdf7300d5aadacb7d5c81d6793a6b6f3166a11b8b40ea1a392b00d3f084daeef" :answer/id #uuid "13e78480-ee22-5173-91c1-676584a8a64b" :answ